- learn from the Materials and independently apply the knowledge gained from them;
- use general ideas, concepts, principles, techniques, security patterns, remediation approaches, and engineering knowledge learned from the Materials in your own work;
- independently create, modify, adapt, or implement code and configurations inspired by or based on knowledge learned from the Materials;
- use your independently created implementations in personal, internal, professional, commercial, or production environments.

Nothing in this License prevents you from applying general knowledge or independently implementing security patterns learned from the Materials.

You are responsible for reviewing, testing, adapting, validating, and securing any implementation used in a development, commercial, or production environment.

